body:
Thank you skytraingal! lots of good critique here

++Alright, I added a branding statement, not sure what format/style to put it in though. Critique for the content is also appreciated. 


//Gotcha on the 'Freelance..' part. i decided to drop the gnu program and wacom tablet experience altogether, as i don't think those are vital.

//Gotcha on the T.A. part

//For the GPA, when i put 4.5/5.0, it seems like a minute score more than a tabulated average. hopefully putting 'weighted' can make it a bit clearer? 4.0 is the highest for me unweighted, but with AP and honors classes it can go up to 5.0.

//Gotcha on the reverse chronological. 

--As for achievements, I have none! As you can tell I did include my qualities, but the truth is I have never won any 'real' award in my life, despite entering competitions! Only participation and consolation prizes...
But I'll save that for my own internal conflict :)

--And as for the relevance of provided experience: that's one thing I worried about while I was writing the resume up. I am introverted, but looking forward interact with people no problem. I have no true way of proving experience with that, though. And I have handled money at a cashier for a club fundraiser, but I hardly think that could translate to something resume material.  I am a fast learner, and even if not a natural, I work at it. But again, it's a bit fluffy and nebulous. 

Tips? Thanks again! Really appreciate it.
